            "Description":"A failure in the wheel speed sensor (Requirement 25) could lead to a situation where the Traction Control System (Requirement 74) is unable to function as intended, potentially causing safety issues."
         }
      ],
      "Recommendations":[  
         {  
            "Action":"Implement Redundant Sensors",
            "Description":"To mitigate the risk of sensor failure impacting traction control, consider implementing redundant wheel speed sensors. This ensures that if one sensor fails, others can provide necessary data to maintain system functionality."
         },
         {  
            "Action":"Enhance Fail-Safe Mode",
            "Description":"Ensure that the fail-safe mode activated during a sensor failure (Requirement 25) is robust enough to support basic traction control functions or at least minimize risk until the issue is resolved."
