{  
   "requirements": [  
      {  
         "ID": 66,
         "description": "Vehicle acceleration must be linear and proportional to the displacement of the acceleration sensing to provide a smooth and controlled driving experience.",
         "implications": [
            "The vehicle's control system should ensure that any change in accelerator pedal position results in a corresponding, predictable change in acceleration.",
            "This requires precise calibration of sensors and actuators involved in measuring pedal displacement and controlling engine output."
         ],
         "challenges": [
            "Achieving linearity across the entire range of pedal positions can be difficult due to mechanical and electronic variances.",
            "Environmental factors such as temperature changes may affect sensor accuracy, requiring compensation mechanisms."
         ]
      },
      {  
         "ID": 7,
         "description": "The system must continuously monitor the accelerator pedal sensor for failures and respond appropriately when a fault is detected.",
         "implications": [
            "A robust diagnostic system needs to be in place to detect anomalies or malfunctions in real-time.",
            "Upon detecting a fault, the system should have predefined responses such as alerting the driver, switching to a safe mode, or disabling certain functionalities."
         ],
         "challenges": [
            "Ensuring that false positives do not trigger unnecessary alerts or actions is crucial for maintaining user trust and safety.",
            "The system must be capable of distinguishing between different types of faults (e.g., sensor failure vs. temporary disconnection) to respond appropriately."
         ]
      }
   ],
   "integrationConsiderations": [
      "Both requirements emphasize the need for high reliability and precision in sensor technology and control algorithms.",
      "Integration of these systems should consider redundancy and fail-safes to enhance safety and performance.",
      "Testing under various conditions is essential to ensure that both linearity and fault detection perform as expected."
   ]
}

